# Environment variables for @ostomy/web.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to client code; nothing here is
# a secret (a public SPA client cannot hold one) — the PKCE flow this app
# uses (apps/web/src/auth) exists specifically so no client secret is
# needed. Copy to .env.local for local development; never commit .env.local.

# Standard OIDC issuer. Discovery is fetched from
# ${VITE_OIDC_ISSUER}/.well-known/openid-configuration — see
# apps/web/src/auth/discovery.ts. In development this points at the
# mock-oauth2-server container's patient issuer (apps/api/.env.example's
# OIDC_ISSUER); in production it points at the patient Cognito user pool's
# hosted UI domain.
VITE_OIDC_ISSUER=http://localhost:8090/patient-issuer

# This SPA's own registered OIDC client id — distinct from
# apps/api/.env.example's OIDC_AUDIENCE (the API's resource identifier).
VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=ostomy-web

# The API's resource identifier, sent as the `audience` request parameter on
# both the authorization redirect and every token exchange.
#
# MUST equal apps/api/.env.example's OIDC_AUDIENCE. JwtAuthGuard validates
# `aud` against that value, so a mismatch means sign-in succeeds and then
# every single API call returns 401 — a failure whose cause is three layers
# from its symptom. Code review caught exactly that: this file already said
# the client id is "distinct from the API's resource identifier", and the
# code then never sent the resource identifier at all.
#
# An issuer that expects `resource` rather than `audience` (RFC 8707) needs a
# change in apps/web/src/auth/, not a different value here.
VITE_OIDC_AUDIENCE=ostomy-patient-app

# Optional. Scopes requested at authorization; defaults to "openid profile".
#
# Deliberately NOT including `offline_access`: it is not a scope Cognito
# supports, and requesting it makes the hosted UI return
# `error=invalid_scope` so sign-in never completes. Cognito issues refresh
# tokens from app-client configuration instead. Set this only for an issuer
# that needs something beyond the portable default.
# VITE_OIDC_SCOPE=openid profile

# Must exactly match a redirect URI registered with the issuer, and must be
# a route this app actually handles — the app root, so the callback lands
# on the (auth-guarded) physician view rather than an unmatched route.
VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/

# Origin the API is served from, no trailing slash.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional. Where the issuer returns the browser after RP-initiated logout
# (OpenID Connect RP-Initiated Logout 1.0 §2); defaults to the app's own
# origin.
#
# Must be registered with the issuer as a post-logout redirect URI. An
# unregistered value makes the end_session_endpoint refuse the request — so
# signOut clears local tokens BEFORE redirecting, and a refusal downgrades
# to a local-only sign-out rather than leaving the session intact.
# VITE_OIDC_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/

# Optional. Minutes of inactivity before the session ends; defaults to 15.
# Set to 0 to disable the timer.
#
# This is a shared-workstation control, not a token-lifetime one: a valid
# access token says nothing about whether the person who signed in is still
# the person at the keyboard. A clinic workstation left unattended on the
# physician view is showing one patient's stoma output to whoever sits down
# next.
# VITE_SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=15
